              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "**Mundra Port** is the **largest commercial and container port in India**. Here are the key details about it:\n\n### 1. Location\n* **Where:** It is located on the northern shores of the Gulf of Kutch near the town of Mundra, in the Kutch district of **Gujarat, India**. \n\n### 2. Ownership and Operation\n* **Operator:** It is owned and operated by **Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone Limited (APSEZ)**, a subsidiary of the Adani Group. \n* **Significance:** It was India's first private port and has grown to become the flagship port of the Adani Group.\n\n### 3. Key Features & Capabilities\n* **Deep-Draft & All-Weather:** It is a deep-draft, all-weather port, which allows it to handle massive ocean-going vessels, including ultra-large container ships (such as the *MSC Anna*, one of the largest container ships to ever dock in India).\n* **Coal Terminal:** It houses the world's largest import coal terminal.\n* **Cargo Capacity:** The port handles a vast array of dry bulk, liquid cargo, crude oil, and containers. It recently made history by becoming the first Indian port to handle over **200 million metric tonnes (MMT) of cargo** in a single year.\n* **Special Economic Zone (SEZ):** The port is integrated with a multi-product Special Economic Zone, making it a major industrial and logistics hub.",
